  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/Thorium/fsharp-refactor",
  "published": "2026-11-13T15:15:14.663Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.8.54: --exclude-codes leaves rules out of a run, after --codes and --categories and ahead of fsharprefactor.json; the MCP analyze call takes excludeCodes.\n\n 0.8.53: A compilation that finished keeps its fixes when Ctrl+C or a file error comes before the next framework's pass. Ctrl+C exits 130, never a stack trace. An empty or comment-only fsharprefactor.json refuses nothing. --mcp answers a refused call with its own reason. A generator's banner is read at the end of a header line and below an attribute of several lines. A glob ignores case on macOS.\n\n 0.8.52: Reads code with FSharp.Compiler.Service 43.12.402 (FSharp.Analyzers.SDK 0.41), the compiler of FsAutoComplete 0.86.\n\n 0.8.51:A run that fails or is interrupted (Ctrl+C) puts back the compilation in progress; a source that cannot be written costs that compilation, not a crash. A fsharprefactor.json that is no JSON, a --report into a missing directory, `--report --dry-run` and filters that leave no rule are refused before anything is written. A glob searches the directories it names (`src/App*/*.fsproj` swept all of `src`). A single named file gets no --api-changes reshapes. --mcp works inside the directory it is given or started in and writes nothing outside it, applies nothing under --dry-run, validates `codes` and `categories` and survives a malformed request. Prose such as \"types generated by JsonProvider\" no longer marks a file generated.\n\n 0.8.50: FR0029's return hoist no longer takes the `elif` links after an awaiting arm as a branch of their own: it put `return` in front of the `elif` keyword, which didn't compile, and the build check rolled the edit back.\n\n 0.8.49: FR0016 and FR0070 read what takes reference types only (a value, a record literal or a type argument given to it), in the project's other files and, under --api-changes, the projects referencing the type: [<Struct>] stopped TryAddSingleton compiling.\n\n 0.8.48: New rules FR0183, and FR0184 (off by default): secrets and clients a redirect exposes. New rule FR0185 (off by default): unions with no fields can be structs. FR0016, FR0070, FR0130, FR0131, FR0011, FR0033, FR0026 and FR0132 read past harmless attributes. FR0118 leaves shared and detached work, comparisons and overloads with another return type alone; FR0152 ignores unrelated removals.",
